abstract: >-
  The Knowledge Lifecycle names how a large language model acquires, stores,
  retrieves, updates and forgets knowledge, and this repository measures what
  breaks where retrieval meets update: a document in the prompt that
  contradicts what the model learned. Across 864 forward passes on six open
  models from 124M to 1.5B parameters, holding a fact rises with size at every
  step, from 25.0% to 98.6%, while deferring to the document follows no such
  order. Every result is read at the rank of the answer, which is what the
  model would actually say, and every number comes from one deterministic
  script that runs on an ordinary CPU. The repository holds the preprint
  (viXra:2611.0038), the framework manuscript, the measurement code, a live
  demonstration and the explainer video.
